 "gossip": {
  "text": "Lamar Jackson is officially out. The ankle that was \"questionable\" in yesterday's column has ruled him out for a second straight week, so Tyler Huntley starts in Cleveland. Waiting on the other sideline is Todd Monken, the Ravens' own former offensive coordinator, who the Ravens believe wants \"to kick our tail.\" Cam Jurgens has gone from questionable to out with his concussion, and Broderick Washington Jr. and Matt Hibner are out too. The line that opened at 6.5 is now 3. Yesterday I said I was with the market. The market kept walking, and I'm still with it. Kyle Hamilton says everybody has \"the utmost confidence\" in Huntley, which is the kind of thing teammates say. Rob and Darren have four bets on a backup quarterback facing a coach who knows the playbook. My hunch: Monken has been waiting for this one.\n\nSteve, don't get smug. Rashee Rice is now officially out against the Chargers, tackle Josh Simmons is out with a back injury and L'Jarius Sneed is questionable. Still, Kansas City is a 7.5-point favourite against a team that hasn't won a game, and I think the Chiefs stay unbeaten. Steve holds them against all three of his friends, so he's the one sitting pretty.\n\nAndy, your Lions are on a bye and still put three players on injured reserve: Ben Bartch, Devin White and Tom Kennedy. That's quite something for a week off. Darren, ESPN says your Bengals are \"overperforming.\" I know you'll read that as a compliment. Rob is 62% on that bet and won't.",
  "written": "2026-10-17T06:16:19-07:00",
  "based_on": 19
 }
}